title: Fundraising
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: fundraising_timer <= 0
on-arrival: fundraising_timer = 12

= Fundraising

The campaign never ends, and neither does the need for money. Where do we turn?

- @small_dollar: Small-dollar drive
- @big_donors: Courting major donors
- @grassroots_events: Grassroots house parties
- @easy_discard

@small_dollar
subtitle: +2 resources, +1 annual dues
unavailable-subtitle: Needs time.
on-arrival: resources += 2; dues += 1*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent -= 2; biz_relation -= 1; month_actions += 1

Millions of small donations roll in, powered by grassroots outrage and relentless emails. The base feels ownership.

@big_donors
subtitle: +3 resources; business happy, left angry
on-arrival: resources += 3; biz_relation += 5; progressive_dissent += 5; left_relation -= 3; month_actions += 1

Dinners in the Hamptons and Silicon Valley fill the war chest. Progressives complain about who is buying access.

@grassroots_events
subtitle: +1 resource, +enthusiasm
on-arrival: resources += 1; dem_enthusiasm += 0.6; labor_dissent -= 2; month_actions += 1

Living-room fundraisers and union-hall suppers are slower but build loyalty.
